  "description_snippet": "VULNERABILITY DETAILS\n\nThe `String::Value` constructor stores the length of the incoming String object into its `length_` member, an `uint32_t`. Then it makes an allocation from PartitionAlloc for `length_ + 1`, which can overflow to zero if the length of the incoming String is UINT32_MAX.\n\n```cpp\nS"
